# A local that is a slot of the root and a cell of a closure's sub-body
# (`storage sub 0: slot`, `storage sub 1: cell`): known-null reads each
# sub-body's own storage row, so the root's whole move of it empties it
# and the `Drop` after the move goes (the bench `points` shape). A move
# of a heap cell keeps its drop, which ends the box (`rounds_cell`).
fn eat(s: string) -> usize:
    s.len()
